    {
      "id": "1560159441125376001",
      "type": "Reply",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-15T05:16:37.125+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "I'm looking forward to getting a bond tester unit with a \"programmable precision voltage supply\" add-on \"dongle\" (the dongle made and ordered; the tester with the dongle programmed) to do retention (and with it, power-up-bit-pattern) tests on some of the dies (especially if I can get the dongle to someone who has a bond tester unit and access to a bunch of the dies and time to cycle a few dozen through it (technically should only take like 5 minutes or thereabouts at a single temperature)).\nThat's for FlexMem, Stef's SRAM generator. \nTechnically that covers 5V and two DRC variants of 3.3V SRAM.\nAnd it's pretty much the densest flexible/varied SRAM we have access to without signing any NDAs.",
      "author": {
        "id": "262706220073222144",
        "name": "namibj",
